From 251462065928dcb0a82130b31cb3f1e23686f30c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unxed <unxed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:25:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/48] asm_amd64: skip the software m0.tls self-check on Hurd,
 like Solaris/illumos/Haiku

Root cause of the early SIGTRAP (runtime.abort at rt0_go, before any Go
code -- not even osinit -- ran): rt0_go's generic TLS bootstrap writes
0x123 through the real hardware %fs-based g-slot (via settls/get_tls,
which for us -- like Solaris/illumos/Haiku -- is just the negative-offset
glibc trick) and then compares it against the *software* runtime.m0.tls
static variable, which is never written on these platforms since they
don't use the software TLS path at all. That comparison can never succeed
for a glibc/%fs-based port, so it aborted on literally every run,
before any of our own code (osinit, newosproc, minit -- all confirmed via
debug prints that never fired) executed. Missing from the GOOS_haiku/
GOOS_solaris/etc. skip-list here was simply an oversight when porting the
Haiku pattern; every other place needed for the port doesn't have this
class of bug since it's the only self-test of its kind in the runtime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015F6Vb87BFK4j9tVQhdKr9H
---
 src/runtime/asm_amd64.s | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/runtime/asm_amd64.s b/src/runtime/asm_amd64.s
index f5131cce..f0bcf0de 100644
--- a/src/runtime/asm_amd64.s
+++ b/src/runtime/asm_amd64.s
@@ -274,6 +274,12 @@ needtls:
 	// skip TLS setup on Haiku
 	JMP ok
 #endif
+#ifdef GOOS_hurd
+	// skip TLS setup on Hurd: TLS is entirely glibc/pthread's, accessed via
+	// the negative-offset %fs trick (same as Solaris/illumos/Haiku), not
+	// through this software m0.tls self-check.
+	JMP ok
+#endif
 #ifdef GOOS_openbsd
 	// skip TLS setup on OpenBSD
 	JMP ok
