From a75833e6a07f84fa5e330e9ad192cbe8f475ed6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unxed <unxed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:15:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/48] runtime: make signal-handler register changes take
 effect on Hurd

glibc passes SA_SIGINFO handlers a *copy* of the context (fill_ucontext) and
__sigreturn restores from the struct sigcontext in the same frame, so async
preemption and sigpanic injection (both rewrite RIP/RSP) were silently
ignored. sigtramp now hands the sigcontext to sighandlerhurd, which writes
the changed registers back (after checking that the sigcontext still mirrors
the registers it was given). Measured with poc/ctx_poc.c: sc_r8 is at
offset 32. Adds the t_panic test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
